//? Title: Vincenty inverse: actual longitude iteration and unresolved cases
//? Subtitle: Actual native state and retained original experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Distances on an ellipsoidal Earth differ from spherical great-circle distances.
Vincenty solves an auxiliary-longitude fixed point, but its inverse iteration
can fail near antipodal pairs.
)

\toc

> The method

Reduced latitude is U=atan((1−f)tan(phi)), with WGS84 a=6378137m and
f=1/298.257223563. Auxiliary longitude lambda is iterated from the reduced
observed longitude difference using the ellipsoidal correction. The final arc
sigma and flattening series give s=b*A*(sigma−deltaSigma). The actual successive
lambda updates below expose the stopping condition |delta lambda|<tol. This is
an angular fixed-point criterion rather than a certified metre-error bound; cap
exhaustion yields an unresolved NaN distance.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/vincenty_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::vincenty_work(0, 0, 0, 1, 200, 1e-12, 10);
    std::print("| actual lambda before | after | absolute update radians |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n");
    for (auto q : r.steps)
        std::print("|{}|{}|{}|\n", q.before, q.after, q.delta);
    std::print("\nActual equatorial distance {}m; expected a*pi/180 {}m.\n",
               r.result.distance_m, 6378137. * std::numbers::pi / 180);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Equator longitude0 to1 degree");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual updates", r.result.iterations));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual distance {:.3f} m",
                                     r.result.distance_m));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/vincenty_tiny.svg");
}
```
