> Interpretation and limits

Coordinates are finite degrees in the stated latitude/longitude ranges;
longitude differences are normalized modulo360. Coincident poles return zero
independently of longitude. Nonconverged distances are NaN rather than an
uncertified last-iterate distance. Haversine clamps rounding to its valid domain
and is a sphere comparison, not independent ellipsoid ground truth. The WGS84
result agrees with the retained54972.271m reference at the displayed rounding.
This single line is a numerical check, not a global convergence or accuracy
guarantee.

The complete editable C++ programs save figures locally; results contain
ordinary computed Markdown. Selected counters describe actual producer
operations, excluding validation when stated.

> References

- [Vincenty, Direct and inverse solutions of geodesics on the ellipsoid|https://doi.org/10.1179/sre.1975.23.176.88]

